WHY THIS IS OPEN AT ALL
-----------------------

The claim this project makes is that you can verify its numbers without
trusting whoever published them. That claim is only true if the code computing
them is readable. A closed corpus asking you to believe its calibration scores
would be worth nothing; the openness is not a concession, it is the product.

The same holds for adoption. Cairn asks an agent to consult a corpus when it
gets stuck, and an instruction to consult an opaque service and act on what it
returns is exactly the failure recorded here as cairn-0014. The security story
requires that anyone can read what they are pointing their agent at.


